+# Lumus Desk
+
+An early Linux-first desktop fork **based on OpenCode**. Not an official OpenCode release.
+
+Upstream: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode
+Base commit: `80d43eb7073da9b1763840eb2e1ba778064e2ee3`
+OpenCode's MIT license and copyright are preserved in `LICENSE`.
+
+## Current state
+
+This is source code for an early patch, **not a finished release or a downloadable installer**.
+
+Verified in a local Linux Electron development window:
+- A visible RU/EN button changes the interface language.
+- A theme picker uses OpenCode's existing theme engine, with a new Lumus palette.
+- Light/dark switching changes the visible application colors.
+- An isolated Lumus Desk identity and local backend start, separate from OpenCode's desktop data.
+- The upstream desktop updater is disabled.
+
+Checks: 9 scoped theme tests passed; the UI package typecheck passed. Full desktop/app typechecking did not finish within the available time; production bundling was killed in a 2 GB environment. The general UI test suite had 3 JSX-runtime errors. These are not green release checks.
+
+Not implemented or not verified:
+- Custom command editor and the web-brain / model-hands workflow.
+- Automated Gemini, ChatGPT or Claude web connections.
+- Linux AppImage/deb packages and a Windows installer.
+- Terminal palette behavior, full restart persistence, and a Windows runtime test.
+- Complete rebranding, separate icons and a full telemetry audit.
+
+## Linux development (including Arch-based systems)
+
+The inherited stack is Bun + TypeScript + SolidJS + Electron, with electron-vite and electron-builder. Use a current Bun and Node.js. Electron requires the usual Linux desktop libraries; this is not a headless CLI app. No package-manager command below installs system dependencies or uses sudo.
+
+```sh
+bun install --frozen-lockfile
+cd packages/desktop
+node node_modules/electron/install.js
+bun ./scripts/copy-icons.ts dev
+# Local source backend, not the upstream downloaded service:
+export OPENCODE_CHANNEL=local
+export OPENCODE_VERSION=2.0.0-lumus-local
+export OPENCODE_DESKTOP_SERVER_CHANNEL=local
+export OPENCODE_DESKTOP_CLI_DEV="$(cd ../cli && pwd)"
+# In the limited-memory test environment this avoided the bundled dev mode.
+export LUMUS_LOW_MEMORY_DEV=1
+node node_modules/electron-vite/bin/electron-vite.js dev
 ```
 
-> [!TIP]
-> Remove versions older than 0.1.x before installing.
+These commands describe the path used for the local Linux launch. They are not an Arch packaging recipe. Prefer a normal desktop session and keep Electron sandboxing enabled. No advice to run this application as root.
 
-### Desktop App (BETA)
+AppImage/deb are the intended Linux distribution targets, but **no build artifact is provided yet**. Windows is secondary and untested. A release needs a matching locally built CLI, a successful desktop build, packaging checks and a real startup test before an install command can be recommended. Do not use the upstream OpenCode installers to install Lumus Desk.
 
-OpenCode is also available as a desktop application. Download directly from the [releases page](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/releases) or [opencode.ai/download](https://opencode.ai/download).
